Documentation of the change build.ps1 applies to Execution/ConformExecutor.cs (applied
in-place at build time via anchored replacement, then reverted; for review, not git apply).

Checkpoint workspaces would otherwise land in the "managed workspace" bucket and be conformed
through PerforceExecutor.ConformAsync (real p4 operations, which fail against the Checkpoint
pseudo-cluster). This routes them through the generic materializer-based conform instead, which
resolves CheckpointWorkspaceMaterializer by the Method name and calls its ConformAsync.

--- a/Drivers/JobDriver/Execution/ConformExecutor.cs
+++ b/Drivers/JobDriver/Execution/ConformExecutor.cs
@@
+				List<RpcAgentWorkspace> checkpointWorkspaces = pendingWorkspaces
+					.Where(x => String.Equals(PerforceExecutor.GetMaterializerName(x.Method), CheckpointWorkspaceMaterializer.TypeName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
+					.ToList();
+
 				List<RpcAgentWorkspace> managedWorkspaces = pendingWorkspaces
 					.Where(x => !String.Equals(PerforceExecutor.GetMaterializerName(x.Method), PerforceExecutor.Name, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
+					.Where(x => !checkpointWorkspaces.Contains(x))
 					.ToList();
@@
 					if (perforceWorkspaces.Count > 0)
 					{
 						_logger.LogInformation("Conforming PerforceMaterializers...");
 						await PerforceExecutor.ConformMaterializersAsync(_materializerFactories, _workingDir, perforceWorkspaces, removeUntrackedFiles, workspaceMetadataDirs, _tracer, _logger, cancellationToken);
 					}
+					if (checkpointWorkspaces.Count > 0)
+					{
+						_logger.LogInformation("Conforming Checkpoint workspaces...");
+						await PerforceExecutor.ConformMaterializersAsync(_materializerFactories, _workingDir, checkpointWorkspaces, removeUntrackedFiles, workspaceMetadataDirs, _tracer, _logger, cancellationToken);
+					}
